        [
          "Liu Bolin is an artist from China who is now famous ",
          {
            "itemId": "1"
          },
          " countries all over the world. He’s called the ‘Invisible Man’ because in his pictures it’s very hard to see him."
        ],
        [
          "Liu ",
          {
            "itemId": "2"
          },
          " in Shandong, China, in 1973. He studied at the Shandong College of Art, and then he went to the Central Academy of Fine Arts in Beijing."
        ],
        [
          "He ",
          {
            "itemId": "3"
          },
          " and works in Beijing, but he ",
          {
            "itemId": "4"
          },
          " travels to other countries and he’s shown his work in Asia, Europe and America. In this photo, Liu ",
          {
            "itemId": "5"
          },
          " in front of some logs. He’s in the ",
          {
            "itemId": "6"
          },
          " of the photo, and if you look carefully, you can see his ",
          {
            "itemId": "7"
          },
          " and jacket."
        ],
        [
          "Liu’s photos can take ten hours to prepare. He chooses a place to stand, and then his assistant ",
          {
            "itemId": "8"
          },
          " him paint his clothes and his face. When everything is ready, his assistant takes the photo. The results are amazing – sometimes people who are ",
          {
            "itemId": "9"
          },
          " past him in the street don’t know that he’s there."
        ],
        [
          "Liu’s work is popular because it’s different and fun, but his work also has a ",
          {
            "itemId": "10"
          },
          " message: he wants people to think about the world around them."
